                "goldenRule": "Hypertension in ICP is a survival mechanism to perfuse the brain. Do not simply lower it.",
                "mnemonic": {
                    "title": "Cushings Triad",
                    "content": "1. High BP (Widening Pulse Pressure)\n2. Low HR (Bradycardia)\n3. Low RR (Irregular/Cheyne-Stokes)",
                    "explanation": "These 3 signs indicate increased intracranial pressure (ICP) is crushing the brainstem."
                },
                "cheatSheet": {
                    "title": "ICP Warning Signs",
                    "points": [
                        "Widening Pulse Pressure (Systolic UP, Diastolic Steady/Down)",
