                        "Avoid Lumbar Puncture (Risk of herniation)",
                        "Keep Head of Bed at 30 degrees (Promote drainage)"
                    ]
                },
                "referenceInfo": {
                    "anatomy": "The cranium is a fixed box containing Brain (80%), Blood (10%), and CSF (10%). (Monro-Kellie Doctrine).",
                    "physiology": "When injured, the brain swells. To fight the pressure, the body raises BP to force blood into the brain (Cerebral Perfusion Pressure). The baroreceptors then lower HR in response to the high BP.",
                    "pharm": "Mannitol (Osmotic Diuretic) pulls fluid out of the brain tissue into the blood to be excreted, lowering ICP."
                },
                "difficulty": {
